# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the host KV tier SHIP-CANDIDATE gates (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of
# tp4/prefix-tiers and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. Templates only: no tag is pushed from the
# branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the pass rule. ONE IMAGE: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-tier-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed tp4/prefix-tiers head
# (sed -i 's/tp4-fusion-tier-1/<tag>/' *.env). The cards are under development: nothing here stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# TC5 (TIMED, the ABAB's second B): the LEVER repeated, as TC3 (profile c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-tierfx-traffic, the host tier on): the same scenario as TC1 with no audit instrument (c2_prefix_gate.py --plan tier-concurrent-timed, scenario tier_concurrent_timed: no row digests, no extent audit; the tier profile's own audits are off),
# timed. THE ABAB: TC2 control, TC3 tier, TC4 control, TC5 tier, every boot a fresh reset, NO CI load while it runs (the round times are timings; pause the ARC runner sets as the combined window does).
# READ each: the plan verdict PASS (the stall budget is JUDGED here: no seat waited longer than the Lever N decode gap floor, 8 s, between two tokens in any window), then the four together:
# python3 scripts/ci/tier_concurrent_compare.py <TC2 results> <TC3 results> <TC4 results> <TC5 results> (A control, B tier, C control repeat, D tier repeat): exit 0 needs every seat IDENTICAL over its common tokens
# (the seven streams unchanged by the tier), the returning, long-prompt and cold-twin answers IDENTICAL across the profiles, and no longest wait over the budget; it prints, window by window, the round p50/p99 of
# each arm, the TIER arm's p99 against the CONTROL arm's (percent: the number the owner decides on; this pack sets no threshold) and the control-to-control FLOOR (TC2 against TC4). Read each arm's own
# 'round p99 vs control' as the stall of an event, not the tier's cost: the seats grow by their own decode, so a later window is slower whatever happens beside it.
# Duration (estimate): 50 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset prefix
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-tier-1
C2_PREFIX_PLAN=tier-concurrent-timed
C2_PREFIX_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-tierfx-traffic
C2_PREFIX_BASELINE=none
C2_BOX_MINUTES=90
